{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nADR 0122 adopts `amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0` for similar-ticket embeddings, and names the IAM gap as a deployment precondition rather than a follow-up. `infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf` grants `bedrock:InvokeModel` only for Anthropic Claude: the statement `ConverseAnthropicClaudeOnly` (`:10`) lists exactly two resource ARNs (`:16-17`), both `anthropic.claude-*`. A tree-wide search finds no Titan or embedding ARN anywhere under `infra/`. The embedding call is therefore denied from the Gerrit instance role today, so the index cannot be built anywhere but a developer's own credentials. ADR 0122 records that the benchmark missed this because it ran under a local principal that already had Titan access.\n\nThis blocks its sibling children: the index subsystem cannot run its embedding step in a deployed environment, and create-time surfacing cannot meet its production criteria, until this lands and is applied.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd the Titan embedding ARN to the existing statement's resource list, and rename the statement and its header comment to match what it then grants. One statement, one policy document, one place to read the role's Bedrock reach.\n\nRestricting this role to Claude is not a constraint the system requires, so there is no reason to carry a second statement to preserve it. ADR 0059's \"The region is wildcarded; the MODEL is not\" is an explanation of why the *region* field carries a wildcard — a cross-region inference profile invokes the foundation model in its member regions — not a requirement that the model stay pinned to one vendor. Splitting the grant in two to keep a vendor name true would add a mechanism to protect a property nothing depends on.\n\nThe statement's existing actions are kept as they are. `bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream` is inert for an embedding call, which is a single request/response, but it is already granted on this statement and removing it from the Claude ARNs is not this ticket's work.\n\nScope the new resource to the one model ARN, `arn:aws:bedrock:*::foundation-model/amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0`, with the region field wildcarded for the same reason the Claude ARNs wildcard it (`:16`). No inference-profile ARN is added: a profile ARN exists for cross-region Converse routing, and the embedding call is a direct foundation-model invocation.\n\n**Verification is a real call, not a policy simulator.** `infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md` (\"How NOT to verify\") and ADR 0059 both record that the simulator answers what the policy language permits for the action you named, not which action the service actually checks, and that this exact inference was made wrongly once on this system. The attestation below is therefore an invocation from the instance role.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf` — add the Titan embedding ARN to the resource list; rename the sid from `ConverseAnthropicClaudeOnly` to `InvokeRebarBedrockModels`; update the header comment at `:4` that describes the intent as \"constraining the Anthropic model\".\n- `infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md` — `:13` names `aws_iam_role_policy.bedrock_converse` as the grant; record that it now also admits the embedding model, reached by direct foundation-model invocation rather than a profile.\n- `docs/adr/0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md` — its IAM paragraph states \"IAM is scoped to Claude only\", which this change makes false; add a dated pointer to ADR 0122 and this ticket. The surrounding line citations in that paragraph (`iam_s7.tf:57-75`, `:60-63`, `:64-67`) are already stale against the present 26-line file and are left untouched rather than silently re-pointed, because correcting them is not this ticket's work.\n- `evals/similar-tickets/README.md` — `:131` states the review-bot instance role is not Titan-capable; update it to describe the grant once applied.\n- `infra/runbooks/bedrock-ci-oidc.md` — `:130` and `:239` reproduce the sid `ConverseAnthropicClaudeOnly` verbatim for the separate external-CI role, and `:145` states the shape is `iam_s7.tf`'s \"verbatim in shape\". Renaming the sid here breaks that claim; update the runbook to name the new sid and state that the external CI role deliberately does not carry the embedding grant.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo automated test is added. Nothing in the tree asserts the policy document's shape — a tree-wide search for `ConverseAnthropicClaudeOnly` and `bedrock_converse` outside this file returns only prose in runbooks and ADRs — so there is no existing assertion to extend and a new one would pin a declared policy, not a live grant. ADR 0059 states the limitation directly: \"nothing verifies they were APPLIED before a change lands\", tracked as bug `1c39-96d4-8f9e-4d38`. A test asserting the HCL would therefore produce exactly the false confidence that bug describes. The real check is the live invocation recorded below.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf` grants `bedrock:InvokeModel` on `arn:aws:bedrock:*::foundation-model/amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0` from a single statement that also retains both `anthropic.claude-*` ARNs. Checked by: `grep -c titan-embed-text-v2 infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf` returning 1, `grep -c \"anthropic.claude-\\*\" infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf` returning 2, and `grep -c \"^  statement {\" infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf` returning 1.\n- [ ] No file in the tree still names the sid `ConverseAnthropicClaudeOnly`. Checked by: `grep -rn ConverseAnthropicClaudeOnly .` returning no hits.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on the change. Checked by: the recorded exit status, and Gerrit `Verified +1`.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The grant is applied and proven by a real Bedrock call from the Gerrit instance role, not a policy simulator: an `InvokeModel` against `amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0` returns an embedding vector. Attestation evidence recorded as a comment on this ticket: the Gerrit change number and submitted revision SHA, the UTC timestamp of the invocation, the returned vector's dimension count (expected 1,024 per ADR 0122), and the operator identity that ran it. Checked by: that comment existing with all four fields.\n- [ ] Documentation no longer claims the role is Claude-only: `docs/adr/0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md` carries a dated note pointing at ADR 0122 and this ticket, `infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md` describes the widened grant, `infra/runbooks/bedrock-ci-oidc.md` names the new sid and records that the external CI role has no embedding grant, and `evals/similar-tickets/README.md` no longer states the instance role cannot reach Titan. Checked by: grep for \"scoped to Claude only\" returning no unqualified claim, and each of the four files containing a reference to ADR 0122."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793578694617545813,"uuid":"16680ffd-85df-4d75-b8da-cece8144331a"}